When Systems Catch Fire / 点火 - Layered License Notice

Effective for this distribution version and later modifications that include this notice, this repository uses a layered licensing model. This notice replaces the former single MIT repository-wide notice for current and future distributions only. It does not revoke MIT rights already granted for earlier MIT-licensed versions, earlier commits, old copies, or existing forks.

1. Core executable software

Original core executable software, including runtime tools, validators, executors, Function OS implementations, scripts under `tools/`, workflow implementation code, and other software files not otherwise marked, is licensed under the Business Source License 1.1 as parameterized in `LICENSES/active/BUSL-1.1.md`.

This material is source-available before its Change Date. It must not be described as OSI open source during the BUSL period. On the Change Date for each covered version, it changes to AGPL-3.0-or-later.

2. Original documentation, reports, and copyrightable curated content

Original prose documentation, reports, narrative explanations, and copyrightable curated content are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International, unless a file or directory says otherwise. See `LICENSES/active/CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.md`.

3. Value charter and general governance principles

The life-community value charter and general governance principle texts are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International, unless a file says otherwise. See `LICENSES/active/CC-BY-SA-4.0.md`.

4. Public interfaces and interoperability schemas

Public interface specifications, interoperability schemas, and files explicitly marked as interface/schema assets are licensed under Apache License 2.0. See `LICENSES/active/APACHE-2.0.md`. This grant does not expand to core executable software merely because that software reads or writes a schema.

5. Third-party material and unclear rights

Third-party materials, factual statements, quotations, paper metadata, references, imported exports, and unclear-rights content are not relicensed by inclusion in this repository. Their original rights status remains in force unless separately stated.

6. Historical MIT boundary

The complete pre-121Q9 MIT text is preserved at `LICENSES/legacy/MIT-pre-121Q9.md`. Anyone who obtained earlier MIT-licensed versions may continue to use those versions under MIT, including existing forks. New versions and new modifications distributed with this notice are governed by the layered licenses above.

This licensing notice is not legal advice. Commercial production use beyond the BUSL Additional Use Grant requires a separate commercial license or written reciprocal agreement from the rights holder.
